    {
      "id": "bcb956f0-b3ab-4637-ada9-9b1fef5636d4",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-02-20T12:27:00.000Z",
      "title": "Advani Hotels & Resorts (India) Limited Announces Company Secretary and Compliance Officer Changes",
      "body": "Advani Hotels & Resorts (India) Limited announced that Mr. Deepesh Joishar has tendered his resignation from the position of Company Secretary and Compliance Officer to pursue an alternate career opportunity outside the Organization. He tendered his resignation vide letter dated January 3, 2026 and will be relieved from his responsibilities with effect from close of business hours on February 20, 2026. Advani Hotels & Resorts (India) Limited announced the appointment of Mr. Milind Nigam as Company Secretary and Compliance Officer of the Company with effect from February 21, 2026. Mr. Milind Nigam holds a bachelor’s degree in commerce and master’s degree in law. He is an associate member of the Institute of Company Secretaries of India. He has over 22 years of experience in the secretarial ",
      "keyDevTypeId": "16",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "58d131f3-c780-46b3-8633-d239c8daad52",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-01-25T05:49:27.000Z",
      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹1.17 (vs ₹1.29 in 3Q 2025)",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹1.17 (down from ₹1.29 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹360.9m (up 2.7% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹107.8m (down 9.5% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 30% (down from 34% in 3Q 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 1% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 18% per year, which means it is well ahead of earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
